}_{2}^{2}\\,$ in terms of the components of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})^{2}+(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})-3({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & =8{y}_{1}^{2}-8{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{1}^{2}+3{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2}-3{y}_{1}^{2}-12{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-12{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =7{y}_{1}^{2}-17{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-12{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140936/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f203c9bf-7d12-56db-aafe-6639162eae93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140936"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94134/selection/fe5ffbef6efca03c43f0edd3a50759cc3b0912f57418d33057eef3f6164c7149" :answer/id #uuid "977886e5-dfca-516b-b6c0-d35a1127605e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25{y}_{1}^{2}-9{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94134/selection/425240311004012e6e62a043515bba8d67c221b8a6959a7472d1cab798d76f47" :answer/id #uuid "ef62b86a-d0e0-5900-b2e0-25a6662a40f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{y}_{1}^{2}+12{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94134/selection/69fde8fab6597167785ea4716a4cea2057dfe37d582283034bdb6a444f51f718" :answer/id #uuid "9cfde215-d137-535a-a327-aa06cb6d906f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{y}_{1}^{2}-10{y}_{1}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94134/selection/2d41cacb4080ebc974cf3bdd279acd17471f87d3c05