 "q-140937/selection/f227907eadd5cf3530eaaa6358cfeabf030556c8d4ea43e20b4c16e99f16a592" "q-140937/selection/d339430d7301f8ba7e055d32417a9e7f5110c627ccc618597311067f96f9ef32"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140937" :question/id #uuid "20339293-778c-5bbb-946b-a6ff1065301d" :question/math-academy-id "q-140937" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ in terms of the components of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n  \n\ngives the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({y}_{1})^{2}-4({y}_{1})(-{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2})+3(-{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{1}^{2}-12{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{y}_{1}^{2}-18{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+27{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =8{y}_{1}^{2}-30{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+27{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140937/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f203c9bf-7d12-56db-aafe-6639162eae93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140937"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94171/selection/e88c630280784c889f7e7b1383f6702c20088b5d6d657a001c34f685c0dd4c19" :answer/id #uuid "a3d52dc0-01d2-50f0-a6f6-4a08deacdbab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{y}_{2}^{2}-8{y}_{1}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94171/selection/13c072d0599e319875c207a1e8c494a387c32