 \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ in terms of the components of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy solving the second equation for ${x}_{1}$ and substituting it into the first equation, we obtain the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =(-{y}_{2})^{2}+4(-{y}_{2})({y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={y}_{2}^{2}-4{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-12{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-11{y}_{2}^{2}-4{y}_{1}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94171/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f2a5391-d8bb-5084-941a-bb787e8729f3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94171"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94178/selection/993d13d5aeff954bdc21a46febb0c89bcf8a9f10f3012e36068915882fdb5900" :answer/id #uuid "2210f297-dac2-5381-8765-9b5e5e04bae4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94178/selection/213ea2db7b9562a4ae83489057d08da027ce41723380075df2df63437bccf8dc" :answer/id #uuid "8bcf00d8-5c48-5e84-8be4-f95ac01127eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94178/selection/a9bdebbd6a031d12279fa77a9c8d512e6afa02d8303551ab27782f6820e35f58" :answer/id #uuid "33adcb4b-c2e1-5983-bd70