{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy solving the first equation for ${x}_{1}$ and substituting it into the second equation, we obtain the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-{y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(-{y}_{1})^{2}-6(-{y}_{1})(-2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})+(-2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}-12{y}_{1}^{2}+6{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+4{y}_{1}^{2}-4{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-7{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94178/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f2a5391-d8bb-5084-941a-bb787e8729f3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94178"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94166/selection/ca1949e9170ae9dcbc40faca4b18381edf64d3bfaab95b4b93209dd418111e20" :answer/id #uuid "7f9c0829-f94e-5523-8207-09fd8af703e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}_{1}^{2}-5{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94166/selection/bc50bbd1a6b7b4a0e1d937be7278d93f5f71c0bcabda485b680a8d53f88d3cef" :answer/id #uuid "f81d7b1f-15dd-53e0-b2f4-91e437e941b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5{y}_{1}^{2}-7{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94166/selection/7e3b74db5dfd1a3127b676c679387d45f00b3cafe7439b2415277eacf11fea06" :answer/id #uuid "c0e965d3-ad1a-5ee7-8ce3-283ce1577747" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{1}{y}_{+}{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94166/selection/0d73fa79cddac7e6dd4119df96a18